def find_solution(cost_matrix, lines):
    min_val = float('inf')
    for i in range(len(cost_matrix)):
        for j in range(len(cost_matrix[0])):
            if not any((i, j) in line for line in lines) and cost_matrix[i][j] < min_val:
                min_val = cost_matrix[i][j]
    return min_val
```

7.  If there are zeros covered by the lines, then the solution is the sum of the values in the covered zeros.

    ```python
def calculate_solution(cost_matrix, lines):
